{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/962180-why-do-vampire-shows-always-let-vampires-walk-in-the-sun-lately","id":962180,"title":"Why do vampire shows always let vampires walk in the sun lately ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-02T03:37:42-07:00","id":962180,"title":"Why do vampire shows always let vampires walk in the sun lately ?","content":"A female friend of mine had me watch something call the vampire diaries with her and then something called the originals. It got me thinking why do so many Vampire shows lately seems to always let vampires have some power to walk in the sun ?<br /> <br /> I thought apart of the curse was you could never walk in the day light anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T04:06:25-07:00","id":962186,"title":"","content":"That's actually not usually the case in folklore. The originator of vampires being destroyed by sunlight was the movie <i>Nosferatu</i>, which influenced a lot of vampire media including Anne Rice and Vampire: the Masquerade. If you think about it it makes sense -before the advent of electrict light, being restricted to the hours of darkness effectively cuts you off completely from human society. Dracula for example walks in the sun just fine. He (and many other vampires) are however much more powerful at night -often they can't use their supernatural powers while the sun is up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2082-schleiermacher","name":"Schleiermacher","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T05:41:45-07:00","id":962207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Schleiermacher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/962180-why-do-vampire-shows-always-let-vampires-walk-in-the-sun-lately?p=962186#post962186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before the advent of electrict light, being restricted to the hours of darkness effectively cuts you off completely from human society. Dracula for example walks in the sun just fine. He (and many other vampires) are however much more powerful at night -often they can't use their supernatural powers while the sun is up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, this is the reason. Shifts in vampire narratives happen, in a historical sense, following shifts in real-world perceptions about &quot;the worst thing&quot;, to manifest that worst thing theoretically or literally in the text. THE LOST BOYS is about homosexuality and the lack of a father figure. At other times, the &quot;worst thing&quot; was miscegenation, immigration in general, child sexual abuse, plagues, STDs, and so on (in no order).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T06:33:08-07:00","id":962223,"title":"","content":"Also, filming at night is a pain in the butt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T09:50:23-07:00","id":962345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/962180-why-do-vampire-shows-always-let-vampires-walk-in-the-sun-lately?p=962223#post962223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, filming at night is a pain in the butt.</div> </div> </div> </div>This too.<br /> <br /> The lighting for &quot;night&quot; never looks all that dark, anyway.<br /> <br /> And it's not as new as you think. Take a peek at &quot;Forever Knight&quot; and &quot;Moonlight&quot; and Coppola's &quot;Dracula&quot;. All pre-date things like &quot;Twilight&quot; and &quot;True Blood&quot; and such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T10:23:16-07:00","id":962356,"title":"","content":"Stoker's Dracula, even. Sunlight killing vampires is a newer idea than sunlight not killing vampires, although the latter is coming back into vogue lately. Kinda has been since the turn of the century.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-02-2016, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T10:58:45-07:00","id":962371,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Dracula. And honestly, the only shows letting vampires walking in the sun are Twilight and Vampire Diaries (Originals is the spin-off of the lately). In the VDs vampires are indeed burn in the sun, but witches are capable of making jewelry that's shielding them from that effect. I always wondered if the writers did some Vampire/Mage crossover sometime... The bigger sticking points for me is that vampires are eating and drinking excessive amounts of alcohol and basically acting totally human most of the time.<br /> <br /> Basically, I think certain shows just wanted to ride the vampire hype, but didn't want &quot;proper&quot;, monstrous vampires with real drawbacks and banes, at least not as the protagonists, but cute guys and girls (mostly guys) with superpowers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T11:18:55-07:00","id":962389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/962180-why-do-vampire-shows-always-let-vampires-walk-in-the-sun-lately?p=962371#post962371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The bigger sticking points for me is that vampires are eating and drinking excessive amounts of alcohol and basically acting totally human most of the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I forget where it was (I wanna say it was Spike from Buffy while visiting Joan when he was in his nice phase), but I recall a vampire biting into a hamburger and seemingly to enjoy it. Totally killed the &quot;I am a creature of the night&quot; vibe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T14:22:56-07:00","id":962497,"title":"","content":"I've always assumd it was cause the teens who watch those shows prefer the blade style vampire, who IS a day walker.. Much more cooler.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T14:59:27-07:00","id":962517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/962180-why-do-vampire-shows-always-let-vampires-walk-in-the-sun-lately?p=962345#post962345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This too.<br /> <br /> The lighting for &amp;quot;night&amp;quot; never looks all that dark, anyway.<br /> <br /> And it's not as new as you think. Take a peek at &amp;quot;Forever Knight&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;Moonlight&amp;quot; and Coppola's &amp;quot;Dracula&amp;quot;. All pre-date things like &amp;quot;Twilight&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;True Blood&amp;quot; and such.</div> </div> </div> </div>Slight correction: The sun was definitely harmful in Forever Knight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/231-blitzburger","name":"Blitzburger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar231_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T06:35:58-07:00","id":962797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blitzburger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/962180-why-do-vampire-shows-always-let-vampires-walk-in-the-sun-lately?p=962517#post962517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Slight correction: The sun was definitely harmful in Forever Knight.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yup. Sun was the biggest danger to Nick, next to LaCroix of course. Loved the fact that he worked the night shift as a cop. Only the night shift. Never mind the notion that he'd have to show up for court during the day, etc.<br /> <br /> Maybe his partner went for him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T07:12:08-07:00","id":962809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/962180-why-do-vampire-shows-always-let-vampires-walk-in-the-sun-lately?p=962389#post962389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I forget where it was (I wanna say it was Spike from Buffy while visiting Joan when he was in his nice phase), but I recall a vampire biting into a hamburger and seemingly to enjoy it. Totally killed the &quot;I am a creature of the night&quot; vibe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires could eat and drink freely in Buffy. Didn't do them any good and they still needed blood, but they could enjoy the taste, get drunk, whatever. Never really bothered me personally, since &quot;I can't have normal food&quot; always struck me as pretty insignificant as far as drawbacks of vampirism go, but YMMV.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T08:55:39-07:00","id":962843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/962180-why-do-vampire-shows-always-let-vampires-walk-in-the-sun-lately?p=962497#post962497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always assumd it was cause the teens who watch those shows prefer the blade style vampire, who IS a day walker.. Much more cooler.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, even with the day walking nonsense, tvd had pretty creepy vampires actually","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 09-03-2016, 12:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T10:46:16-07:00","id":962884,"title":"","content":"My novel series I am working on lets vampires walk in the sun, but they can't use their powers and they get kind of weak and sickly if they don't cover all their skin, but they can still (barely) function in the day, even though their biological clocks are skewed toward being nocturnal anyway. I think it strikes a good balance. I also have it so dhampir don't need to sleep at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T11:56:05-07:00","id":962928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/962180-why-do-vampire-shows-always-let-vampires-walk-in-the-sun-lately?p=962223#post962223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, filming at night is a pain in the butt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly this more than really anything else. Its why they had vampires going out during the day in Kindred: the Embraced and why a good portion of Angel takes place indoors but during the day. In addition to the lighting difficulties of setting up night shots there's also the fact that shooting multiple takes for every scene is a long process, and if you're shooting at night that means very late hours. Night time shooting usually entails paying your cast and crew extra, which over a season's worth of episodes is going to substantially drive up the production costs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T17:46:54-07:00","id":963014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/962180-why-do-vampire-shows-always-let-vampires-walk-in-the-sun-lately#post962180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A female friend of mine had me watch something call the vampire diaries with her and then something called the originals. It got me thinking why do so many Vampire shows lately seems to always let vampires have some power to walk in the sun ?<br /> <br /> I thought apart of the curse was you could never walk in the day light anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are thousands of cultures that all have some weird boogeyman that wanders around at night drinking people's blood. The kind of Vampire that can't walk in the sunlight is based on people with porphyria, of which one of the symptons are breaking out into a rash after being in sunlight. Along with a number of freaky mental illnesses.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T20:09:45-07:00","id":963064,"title":"","content":"Isn't the Originals just a prequel to the Vampire Diaries?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T14:17:21-07:00","id":963382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/962180-why-do-vampire-shows-always-let-vampires-walk-in-the-sun-lately?p=963064#post963064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't the Originals just a prequel to the Vampire Diaries?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope - it actually just follows some of the characters that showed up in The Vampire Diaries after they have gone to New Orleans.<br /> <br /> There are flashbacks sometimes, but the bulk of the show is same-time-different-place to Vampire Diaries.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not so noble anymore.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1823-drake","name":"Drake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1823_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"456"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T14:23:55-07:00","id":963384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/962180-why-do-vampire-shows-always-let-vampires-walk-in-the-sun-lately#post962180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A female friend of mine had me watch something call the vampire diaries with her and then something called the originals. It got me thinking why do so many Vampire shows lately seems to always let vampires have some power to walk in the sun ?<br /> <br /> I thought apart of the curse was you could never walk in the day light anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>For those that aren't aware, I feel it is worth pointing out that the vampires in The Vampire Diaries burst into flames and burn away to ash in sunlight - but witches of that universe are capable of enchanting a bit of jewelry, usually a ring, that allows the one vampire it was made for walk unharmed in sunlight while wearing it.<br /> <br /> So that particular universe actually has, in my opinion, a &quot;best of both worlds&quot; approach because it lets the vampires that need it for narrative reasons (such as successfully pulling off pretending not to be a vampire) walk around in daylight, but also provides the opportunity for a vampire to be vulnerable by being &quot;trapped&quot; somewhere unable to escape until nightfall.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not so noble anymore.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1823-drake","name":"Drake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1823_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"456"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T18:02:37-07:00","id":967029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/962180-why-do-vampire-shows-always-let-vampires-walk-in-the-sun-lately?p=962371#post962371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, Dracula. And honestly, the only shows letting vampires walking in the sun are Twilight and Vampire Diaries (Originals is the spin-off of the lately). In the VDs vampires are indeed burn in the sun, but witches are capable of making jewelry that's shielding them from that effect. I always wondered if the writers did some Vampire/Mage crossover sometime... The bigger sticking points for me is that vampires are eating and drinking excessive amounts of alcohol and basically acting totally human most of the time.<br /> <br /> Basically, I think certain shows just wanted to ride the vampire hype, but didn't want &quot;proper&quot;, monstrous vampires with real drawbacks and banes, at least not as the protagonists, but cute guys and girls (mostly guys) with superpowers.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>The Vampire Diaries</i>(and it's spin-off<i>,The Originals</i>\u200b) is based on a book series. The same author also wrote <i>The Secret Circle</i>, another book series about a coven of witches/Mages, that was <b>also</b> made into a show on the CW.(which got canceled after 1 season)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T21:29:13-07:00","id":967148,"title":"","content":"On a side note - I'm not convinced that the title character in the original <b>Dracula</b> novel was actually a vampire. The only people who claimed to see him do anything &quot;supernatural&quot; are the hunters who tracked him down and killed him. And the whole book kind of reads like their excuse for why they did so. Its actually pretty easy to argue they were just a bunch of paranoid conspiracy nuts trying to justify their actions, positing increasingly bizarre interpretations of Dracula's actions in the process.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/962180-why-do-vampire-shows-always-let-vampires-walk-in-the-sun-lately?p=962223#post962223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, filming at night is a pain in the butt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ever listen to the commentary on the <b>True Blood</b> dvds? They go into a lot of detail about the problems of night shoots, and its hilarious - how loopy everyone gets around 3 a.m., and the kind of pranks they start pulling on each other . . . <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T23:02:53-07:00","id":967194,"title":"","content":"One of my favorite authors tends to do things like that. He had three books ostensibly about vampires where it was never actually clear if they were vampires. Very well handled and it made the books much creepier with that doubt.<br /> <br /> But of course he wasn't a vampire, he was the one who created the vampire. Dracula's Monster was the vampire.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">That was a joke.<br /> <br /> More seriously, considering Dracula was the basis for a lot of modern tales that would expand upon what vampires could do, it could just be that he was a vampire but Stoker's idea of vampires was different than ours is.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T00:07:29-07:00","id":967210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/962180-why-do-vampire-shows-always-let-vampires-walk-in-the-sun-lately?p=967194#post967194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of my favorite authors tends to do things like that. He had three books ostensibly about vampires where it was never actually clear if they were vampires. Very well handled and it made the books much creepier with that doubt. (. . .)</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Which author?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T04:56:37-07:00","id":967264,"title":"","content":"In Arabic folklore, <i>gh\u00fbls </i>are strictly daytime monsters. It can leave some people scratching their heads until they realize that in a desert, the day is far, <i>far </i>more dangerous than the night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T08:54:17-07:00","id":967344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PMark</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, I think certain shows just wanted to ride the vampire hype, but didn't want &quot;proper&quot;, monstrous vampires with real drawbacks and banes, at least not as the protagonists, but cute guys and girls (mostly guys) with superpowers.</div> </div> </div> </div>This notion expressed itself in its purest form in a Korean Manhua whose name escapes me now, but was noteworthy for having vampires who literally suffered NONE of the traditional weaknesses, not even the need for blood! They were effectively Beautiful Immortals who, imo, weren't truly &quot;vampires&quot; at all...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/962180-why-do-vampire-shows-always-let-vampires-walk-in-the-sun-lately?p=962797#post962797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yup. Sun was the biggest danger to Nick, next to LaCroix of course. Loved the fact that he worked the night shift as a cop. Only the night shift. Never mind the notion that he'd have to show up for court during the day, etc.<br /> <br /> Maybe his partner went for him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe he used vampiric influence to ensure that all his cases wound up in Night Court? Now, <i>there's</i> a crossover for you!<br /> <br /> (Loved LaCroix, btw...the show really stepped it up a notch when he became a regular, getting a job as a late-night DJ, of all things, spouting poetic musings over the air that just happened to coincide with whatever problem Nick was dealing with that episode...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> Yeah, the Daylight Rings in TVD are a good idea, but I always feel they should be rarer...seems like pretty much ANY vamp of even minor note is sporting one. Didn't they also come up with Moonlight Rings, that enabled werewolves to transform at will and mostly control themselves, instead of only becoming rampaging beasts during the full moon?<br /> <br /> If a Mage in the WoD wanted to create such an artifact for a Kindred, how would you have that work?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T10:19:37-07:00","id":967389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/962180-why-do-vampire-shows-always-let-vampires-walk-in-the-sun-lately?p=967210#post967210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? Which author?</div> </div> </div> </div>Richard Laymon.<br /> <br /> Just off the top of my head. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">There's the Bite, which involves a man called up by his old girlfriend to kill a vampire that's been preying on her at night. The staking goes off successfully, but the majority of the book is about the disposal of the body. The Stake, about a fellow who finds a girl in some ghost town with a stake through her chest, this also has some perspective from a 'vampire hunter,' whose mind seems a bit unbalanced. And the Travelling Vampire Show, a fantastic if dark coming-of-age story where the aforementioned show is a travelling carnival that brings to town the mysteriously lethal Valeria.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T22:29:12-07:00","id":967784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/962180-why-do-vampire-shows-always-let-vampires-walk-in-the-sun-lately?p=967344#post967344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't they also come up with Moonlight Rings, that enabled werewolves to transform at will and mostly control themselves, instead of only becoming rampaging beasts during the full moon?</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bYes, yes they did.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If a Mage in the WoD wanted to create such an artifact for a Kindred, how would you have that work? </div> </div> </div>Devise a Forces spell that works like Mage Armor, to filter out whatever in is about sunlight that burns vampires, then use Prime to Enchant the ring.(or whatever it is) That's how I think it would work in 1E, I don't have 2E, so I can't say. Maybe use Matter, to made SPF 5000 sunscreen?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name